\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Mutual information (MI) between the activation pattern and the input, versus the number of encoding genes $n_\text  {genes}$ for a growing heteromerization index $R/n_\text  {genes}$ ($R$ the number of receptors). $R/n_\text  {genes}\approx 1$ is gene expansion, one gene per receptor. MI grows with the heteromerization index, but the gain per level decays and stays below the perfect reference. Error bars grow with $R$ because the phase space of $\mathbb  {A}$ scales as $2^R$, making the exact entropy intractable. We bracket the Shannon entropy between two bounds : solid lines correspond to an upper-bounded estimate, whereas the dotted lines correspond to a lower-bound, see supplementary material for details.}}{3}{}}
\newlabel{fig:MI}{{2}{3}{}{}{}}
